vendor/ -- what is lifted, from where, and what we changed
==========================================================

The rule (spec.md §12): lifts live here, tracked to a named upstream commit, with local changes
kept as a patch series rather than edited in place. Anything that could not be expressed as a
patch was REWRITTEN into core/ under our own name instead, so this directory stays updatable.
The bottom half of this file is the list of things that went the other way, and why -- that list
is as much a part of the record as the lifts are.

One exception, taken deliberately: the chat lift (common/chat*, the auto-parser, jinja/ and
json-schema-to-grammar) is maintained directly in place. Its former patch series (0002-0021)
was verified applied -- the whole stack reverses cleanly on a copy of the tree it was removed
from, and on the directly edited tree only context lines of 0012 and 0015 have moved -- and the
patch files were then removed: the code itself is the change, the PATCH SERIES notes at the
bottom keep the rationale for each former patch by its old name, and the diffs are in git
history at 008eed4f, the last commit that has vendor/patches/0002-0021. Later changes -- the
render-path work that cut a chat request from three template renders to two and made the
Jinja string machinery move instead of copy -- are likewise direct edits. A refresh of those files is therefore a manual port, not a re-copy and re-apply.

The mechanical half of the promise is vendor/SHA256SUMS: every file under this directory -- lifts,
patch series, this record -- hashed, recomputed by tests/vendor_sums.sh (ctest: vendor_sums). A
file that differs, or arrived unrecorded, fails the suite: an unrecorded change to a lifted
dependency has to survive being a committed, hashed manifest update to ship, not slip through a
rebase. Regenerate the manifest in the same commit that changes vendor/:

    find vendor -type f ! -name SHA256SUMS | sort | xargs sha256sum > vendor/SHA256SUMS

